      "content": "Your concern touches on a long-standing debate in the art world about whether conceptual depth should replace technical mastery. Many critics and historians argue that the \"value\" of contemporary art has always been a complex mix of idea and execution, so political art often demands even higher levels of nuance to avoid being propaganda. The \"skill\" isn't sidelined so much as redefined to include the ability to truthfully and powerfully translate a social issue into a visual language. Ultimately, the most respected contemporary artworks are those that successfully balance a potent political message with undeniable formal beauty and technical craft.",
